.TH AVR\-SERVICE\-TOKEN\-CREATE 1 "" "avr" "Avrea CLI"
.SH NAME
avr-service-token-create \- Create a service token and print its secret once.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B avr service-token create
[OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Create a service token and print its secret once.
.PP
The token belongs to the group --group names, not to you, and keeps working when you leave the organization. It needs at least one grant; every grant is a read and must be within your own access now. The secret is shown once and cannot be retrieved later: store it, for example as a CI secret, and set it as AVR_TOKEN where the token is used. Creating a service token needs a recent sign-in.
.PP
With --json, the selection must include the token field, because the secret cannot be read again. If a --jq filter fails or drops the secret, the command prints the unfiltered JSON instead and exits nonzero, so the secret is not lost.
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
Examples:
    avr service-token create --name ci --group <group-id> --repo acme/api
    avr service-token create --name egress --group <group-id> --all-firewall-rules --ttl 7d
    avr service-token create --name ci --group <group-id> --repo acme/api --json token --jq .token
.fi
.RE
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
JSON FIELDS
    blocked_by, created_at, created_by, expires_at, expiring_soon, grants,
    grants_version, group_id, id, last_used_at, name, organization_id,
    previous_valid_until, revoked_at, revoked_reason, rotated_at,
    rotation_version, status, token
.fi
.RE
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-name\fR \fITEXT\fR
Token name (1-100 characters). (required)
.TP
\fB\-\-group\fR \fITEXT\fR
ID of the group that owns the token (grp-xxx). (required)
.TP
\fB\-\-repo\fR \fITEXT\fR
Grant read access to a repository (org/repo or rep-xxx). Repeatable. (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-firewall\-rule\fR \fITEXT\fR
Grant read access to an egress firewall rule, by rule ID (efr-xxx). Repeatable. (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-all\-firewall\-rules\fR
Grant read access to every egress firewall rule, including rules added later.
.TP
\fB\-\-ttl\fR \fITEXT\fR
Lifetime: e.g. 30m, 8h, 7d, or a number of seconds. 60 seconds to 90 days; the server default is 30 days.
.TP
\fB\-\-never\-expires\fR
The secret never expires: anyone holding it keeps its access until it is revoked. Cannot be combined with --ttl.
.TP
\fB\-\-org\fR \fITEXT\fR
Organization ID or slug. Uses default org if not specified (see: avr config set org).
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR \fITEXT\fR
Output JSON. Pass comma-separated field names, "*" for all fields, or "?" to list available fields.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-jq\fR \fITEXT\fR
Filter --json output through a jq expression.
.SH SEE ALSO
